# Similar Projects and Tools

## 1. The Opportunity Atlas
**Link:** https://www.opportunityatlas.org/

**What it does:** An interactive map that uses U.S. data to show how childhood neighborhoods and demographic factors relate to outcomes such as income and economic mobility.

**How ours is different:** Our project uses side-by-side comparisons of personal traits across several life areas rather than geographic maps.

## 2. Survival of the Best Fit
**Link:** https://www.survivalofthebestfit.com/game/

**What it does:** An interactive hiring game showing how biases in human decisions and training data can be reproduced by AI systems.

**How ours is different:** Our project aims to compare sourced research across multiple types of inequality not just simulate AI bias in hiring.

## Main Takeaway
These projects use games, maps or simulations to explain inequality. Our Project **Same But Different** aims to make demographic differences easy to explore through simple, customizable, side-by-side comparisons with sources and visible data gaps.
